<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Tong Yabghu Khagan</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. c. 630</span> · <a href="/centuries/7th-century">7th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Tong Yabghu <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khagan">Khagan</a> was ruler of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/western-turkic-khaganate">Western Turkic Khaganate</a> from about 618 until his murder around 630. Under him the khaganate reached its greatest extent, collecting tribute from the Sogdian cities and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tokharistan">Tokharistan</a> and fighting the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sasanian-empire">Sasanian Empire</a>. The Buddhist pilgrim <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/xuanzang">Xuanzang</a> met him at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/suyab">Suyab</a> and described his splendid court. His murder by his uncle opened a long civil war among the Western Turks.</p></div>
